          "source_block": 4,
          "candidate_block": 4,
          "candidate_line_count": 7,
          "center_error": 19.933,
          "text": "Article 1 In accordance with the Guiding Opinions on High-Quality Operations\nof the Joint-Stock Company, and in combination with the relevant requirements of\nthe Implementation Rules for High-Quality Operations (Trial) of the Group Company\n(Zhongtu Jingying [2024] No. 341), these Measures are formulated to\ncomprehensively improve project operation quality, effectively manage the\ncompany's domestic operations, and standardize operating procedures and\nworkflows."
        },
        {
          "page": 2,
          "role": "article_text",
          "source_block": 8,
          "candidate_block": 5,
          "candidate_line_count": 4,
          "center_error": 14.587,
          "text": "Article 2 The projects referred to in these Measures include various types of\ncompany business operations such as consulting, surveying, design, supervision, and\ngeneral contracting for engineering projects undertaken through direct commission or\nbidding."
        },
        {
          "page": 2,
          "role": "article_text",
          "source_block": 10,
          "candidate_block": 6,
          "candidate_line_count": 3,
          "center_error": 17.239,
          "text": "Article 3 In principle, the business undertaking process shall follow the\nsequence of project evaluation first, then application for approval, and finally contract\nsigning."
        },
        {
          "page": 2,
          "role": "article_text",
          "source_block": 12,
          "candidate_block": 7,
          "candidate_line_count": 8,
          "center_error": 17.293,
          "text": "Article 4 When carrying out project business undertaking work, factors such as\nthe company's development strategy, business direction, responsibility cost,\nproduction and technical capabilities, and current status shall be comprehensively\nconsidered. According to the process regulations of these Measures, the following\nstages shall be completed: information tracking, project evaluation and application,\nbid document preparation and review, contract negotiation, contract review and\nsigning, owner service during the project implementation phase, and project\nfollow-up visits."
        },
        {
          "page": 2,
          "role": "chapter_heading",
          "source_block": 17,
          "candidate_block": 8,
          "candidate_line_count": 1,
          "center_error": 0.127,
          "text": "Chapter 2 Relevant Responsibilities"
        },
        {
          "page": 2,
          "role": "article_text",
          "source_block": 18,
          "candidate_block": 9,
          "candidate_line_count": 3,
          "center_error": 19.807,
          "text": "Article 5 The Business Development Department is the management\ndepartment for the company's domestic project business operations, responsible for\nthe layout and development of the institute-wide business market."
        },
        {
          "page": 2,
          "role": "article_text",
          "source_block": 20,
